{"messages":[{"role":"system","content":"You are ThreadSense alternatives analyst. You weigh options for a team lead without inventing evidence or clearing review flags.\nYour personal goal is: Compare two or three candidate actions on evidence, applicability and severity fit."},{"role":"user","content":"\nCurrent Task: Compare 2-3 materially different candidate actions for this topic. If the draft proposes an action, include it as the incumbent candidate (incumbent true) with its action_type, instruction, draft_text and rationale copied exactly; include NO_ACTION when observing is plausible. For each operational candidate state intervention_need (kind, why intervening now is needed, evidence) and rate need_strength, temporal_scope (does every current claim rest on current, in-scope sources?), proportionality (is the step proportionate to the evidence and impact?) and list unresolved_assumptions. A source need not literally prescribe a recommendation; a clarification or referral is not wrong merely because questions remain. Set decision: KEEP_INCUMBENT, REPLACE_INCUMBENT (prefer a different candidate that is clearly better) or CLOSE_CALL (close_call true; no winner). For each, cite only evidence_ids present in the evidence provided, and rate evidence support, applicability (current versus historical-only sources) and fit with the assessed severity. Do not invent evidence, outcomes or causes. Refer to people by role (a tutor, the team lead), never by name. Write instruction (one concrete sentence telling the team lead what to do), draft_text (the copyable draft) and rationale (why it helps) in plain words, with no evidence IDs or field names. Name a preferred candidate only if it is clearly better; otherwise set close_call true. Your selection does not resolve the review triggers listed; a team lead decides.\n\nInput JSON:\n{\"topic\": {\"project_id\": \"safety_classification\", \"batch_id\": \"safety_batch_08\", \"candidate_group_id\": \"cluster_691526d72d861e51\", \"topic_id\": \"cluster_691526d72d861e51/topic_1\", \"topic_label\": \"QN rule version reconciliation\", \"projection_gap\": null, \"as_of\": \"2026-10-02T12:00:00Z\", \"member_ids\": [\"member_47ec6cbf3cb791774485e088\", \"member_8fa4d06e2bbd02e4e0e07a2a\"]}, \"draft\": {\"contract_version\": \"agent3-advisor-draft-v11\", \"summary\": \"A QA tutor asks whether a later announcement replaces the old QN trigger; a tutor asks which quarantine rule applies after a recent change. Current guidance settles the fictional-contact exception and identifies the older help-page wording as stale and needing correction.\", \"summary_sentences\": [{\"text\": \"A QA tutor asks whether a later announcement replaces the old QN trigger; a tutor asks which quarantine rule applies after a recent change.\", \"support_claim_ids\": [\"c1\", \"c2\"], \"depends_on\": []}, {\"text\": \"Current guidance settles the fictional-contact exception and identifies the older help-page wording as stale and needing correction.\", \"support_claim_ids\": [\"c4\", \"c5\"], \"depends_on\": []}], \"detail_sentences\": [{\"text\": \"A QA tutor in each thread asks the thread starter to follow a local clarification while saying the conflicting documents still need reconciliation before a general policy update.\", \"support_claim_ids\": [\"c3\"], \"depends_on\": [], \"summary_depends_on\": []}, {\"text\": \"The current instructions exempt clearly fictional contact placeholders alone, require checking that no real individual is identifiable, and preserve review for ambiguous details or separate QN triggers.\", \"support_claim_ids\": [\"c4\"], \"depends_on\": [], \"summary_depends_on\": []}, {\"text\": \"An earlier follow-up records that the instructions and FAQ reflected the clarification, but the older help page still contained the blanket initial-quarantine wording.\", \"support_claim_ids\": [\"c7\"], \"depends_on\": [], \"summary_depends_on\": []}, {\"text\": \"The batch announcement asks for examples in its thread while scope is checked; it does not direct a change to the quarantine rule.\", \"support_claim_ids\": [\"c8\"], \"depends_on\": [], \"summary_depends_on\": []}], \"reasoning\": \"The current instructions and FAQ explicitly establish the narrow supersession, so a new general policy decision is not needed for that branch. The earlier approval is historical authorization, not proof of completion; the later follow-up and current FAQ identify the remaining stale copy. A scoped documentation correction is supported without further research into the general rule. The supplied material does not identify individual tasks whose fictional context or identifiability needs a separate decision.\", \"claims\": [{\"claim_id\": \"c1\", \"kind\": \"INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor reports that the help page still lists an old quarantine trigger and asks whether a later announcement replaces the older note.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790862407.000075\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U014\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790862407.000075\"}], \"quote\": null, \"quote_kind\": \"PARAPHRASE\", \"material\": true}, {\"claim_id\": \"c2\", \"kind\": \"INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A tutor asks which safety quarantine rule applies after the previous week's change.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790924588.000076\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U009\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790924588.000076\"}], \"quote\": null, \"quote_kind\": \"PARAPHRASE\", \"material\": true}, {\"claim_id\": \"c3\", \"kind\": \"INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"Two QA tutors, one in each thread, ask that the local clarification be followed for the case and say the conflicting QN documents still require version reconciliation before a general policy update; these are participant requests, not authoritative instructions.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790862465.000113\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790924634.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U019\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790862465.000113\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U007\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790924634.000113\"}], \"quote\": null, \"quote_kind\": \"PARAPHRASE\", \"material\": true}, {\"claim_id\": \"c4\", \"kind\": \"GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"The current instructions say clearly fictional placeholder contact details alone do not require QN, require checking that no real individual is identifiable, and explicitly replace only the older help page's blanket fictional-contact trigger. Actual identifiable private information still requires review; ambiguous details or separate QN triggers require retaining evidence for review.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:safety-classification-instructions@1.4:1929f0dd\"], \"attributions\": [], \"quote\": null, \"quote_kind\": \"PARAPHRASE\", \"material\": true}, {\"claim_id\": \"c5\", \"kind\": \"GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"The current FAQ confirms that the dated fictional-placeholder clarification supersedes the blanket fictional-contact trigger in QN help page v1.0, states that the older copy has not been rewritten, and directs reporting that stale copy for correction.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:safety-classification-faq@1.1:6025b955\"], \"attributions\": [], \"quote\": null, \"quote_kind\": \"PARAPHRASE\", \"material\": true}, {\"claim_id\": \"c6\", \"kind\": \"HISTORY\", \"text\": \"The earlier approval record records approval of documentation and communication work, with document updates still pending and no observed outcome at approval; it does not establish publication or a standing rule.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:safety-doc-sync-approval@1.0:df877306\"], \"attributions\": [], \"quote\": null, \"quote_kind\": \"PARAPHRASE\", \"material\": true}, {\"claim_id\": \"c7\", \"kind\": \"HISTORY\", \"text\": \"The September 18 follow-up records partial completion: the instructions contained the scoped rule, the FAQ named the supersession, an announcement had been posted, and QN help page v1.0 still contained blanket initial-quarantine wording. It records remaining correction work, not an unresolved general rule or a later repair.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:safety-doc-sync-outcome@1.0:cd4505b9\"], \"attributions\": [], \"quote\": null, \"quote_kind\": \"PARAPHRASE\", \"material\": true}, {\"claim_id\": \"c8\", \"kind\": \"SOURCE_FACT\", \"text\": \"The team lead's October 2 batch announcement notes old QN criteria remaining in a help page and asks for examples in its thread while scope is checked; that directive concerns example collection, not a replacement quarantine rule or an escalation route.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:slack:C_SAFETY_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790937576.000078:4e602f91\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"k:slack:C_SAFETY_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790937576.000078:4e602f91\"}], \"quote\": null, \"quote_kind\": \"PARAPHRASE\", \"material\": true}], \"gaps\": [], \"evidence_sufficiency\": \"SUFFICIENT\", \"proposed_action\": {\"action_type\": \"UPDATE_DOCUMENTATION\", \"intervention_need\": {\"kind\": \"OPERATIONAL_PROBLEM\", \"statement\": \"The older help-page trigger remains identified as stale while a QA tutor and a tutor ask which rule applies, supporting correction of the conflicting reference now.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790862407.000075\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790924588.000076\", \"k:safety-classification-faq@1.1:6025b955\"]}, \"instruction\": \"Correct the older QN help page's fictional-contact branch to match the current instructions, preserving review for identifiable private information and separate triggers.\", \"rationale\": \"The current FAQ explicitly identifies the stale copy and calls for correction. Repairing that reference addresses the documented conflict without reopening the settled, narrowly scoped rule.\", \"draft_text\": \"Contact details: Clearly fictional placeholder contact details alone do not require QN. Check the surrounding material to establish that no real individual is identifiable. Actual identifiable private information still requires review. If details are ambiguous or a separate QN trigger exists, retain the evidence for review.\\n\\nThe September 10 fictional-placeholder clarification replaces the older blanket fictional-contact trigger only. It does not replace unrelated safety controls. Do not extend the fictional-placeholder exception beyond its scope. Use the current Safety Classification instructions and FAQ for this scoped clarification.\", \"scope_note\": \"Change only the older help page's fictional-contact branch; do not broaden the exception or alter unrelated QN controls.\", \"support_claim_ids\": [\"c1\", \"c2\", \"c4\", \"c5\", \"c7\"], \"targets\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"k:safety-doc-sync-outcome@1.0:cd4505b9\", \"section\": \"Remaining work — referenced QN help page v1.0, Contact details\", \"change\": \"CORRECT\"}], \"context_claim_ids\": [\"c3\", \"c6\", \"c8\"]}, \"severity\": {\"level\": \"MEDIUM\", \"rationale\": \"Questions in two threads concern which safety quarantine rule governs, rather than a cosmetic documentation problem. The evidence supports contained uncertainty about handling, but does not show bypassed controls or widespread task disruption.\", \"signals\": [{\"level\": \"MEDIUM\", \"signal_index\": 0, \"signal_text\": \"Recurring confusion about the same rule, tool behavior, or scoring criterion that suggests meaningful workflow or labeling impact\", \"support\": \"A QA tutor asks whether a newer announcement replaces an old quarantine trigger, and a tutor separately asks which quarantine rule applies after a change; both questions concern safety handling.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790862407.000075\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790924588.000076\"]}], \"affected_reporters\": [], \"recurrence\": \"FOUND\", \"recurrence_evidence_ids\": [\"k:safety-doc-sync-outcome@1.0:cd4505b9\"], \"reported_recurrence_evidence_ids\": []}, \"confidence\": 0.92, \"open_confirmation\": \"NONE\", \"open_question\": null, \"open_question_evidence_ids\": [], \"source_conflicts\": [{\"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790862465.000113\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790924634.000113\", \"k:safety-classification-instructions@1.4:1929f0dd\", \"k:safety-classification-faq@1.1:6025b955\"], \"description\": \"The QA tutor replies describe version reconciliation as still needed before a general policy update. For the narrower fictional-contact branch, the current instructions and FAQ already explicitly establish supersession; the replies do not establish that this recorded rule remains undecided.\"}], \"announcement_assessments\": [{\"evidence_id\": \"k:slack:C_SAFETY_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790937576.000078:4e602f91\", \"relevant\": true, \"directive\": true, \"directive_quote\": \"Please keep examples in this thread while we check the scope.\", \"rationale\": \"The announcement concerns the same batch and stale QN criteria. Its directive governs where examples are collected, not which quarantine rule applies or where issues must be escalated.\"}], \"resolution\": [{\"member_id\": \"member_47ec6cbf3cb791774485e088\", \"state\": \"PARTIALLY_RESOLVED\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790862407.000075\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790862465.000113\"], \"basis\": \"A QA tutor receives a case-specific request to follow a local clarification, but the reply does not answer whether the later announcement replaces the older note and still describes reconciliation as needed.\"}, {\"member_id\": \"member_8fa4d06e2bbd02e4e0e07a2a\", \"state\": \"PARTIALLY_RESOLVED\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790924588.000076\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790924634.000113\"], \"basis\": \"A tutor receives a case-specific request to follow a local clarification, but the reply does not spell out the applicable quarantine rule and still describes reconciliation as needed.\"}], \"cove